+From 12079492515d4fa2ed9384077eda065d16b955f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: cioinside <cioinside@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:10:07 +0300
+Subject: [PATCH] fix(server): resolve an issue's live run by issue identity,
+ not by agent
+
+The active-run lookup fell back to the agent's newest running run and
+compared its issue id with the requested one. An agent that works on
+several issues at once owns several live runs, so the fallback always
+answered with a foreign run and the issue looked run-less. A board
+comment with interrupt:true did not interrupt the run, a reassignment
+passed while the old run kept working, and terminalising the issue did
+not stop its run.
+
+Resolve the run by issue identity instead: issue_id, native_issue_id or
+context_snapshot->>'issueId', company scoped, with a running run ordered
+ahead of a newer queued one. The lookup no longer needs an assignee,
+because a run belongs to its issue, not to the currently assigned agent.
